# Teval, Arbiter of Virtue: "Spells you cast have delve" (CR 702.66a, 113.6) - its controller's spells, not an opponent's. Bot1
# casts Teval on turn 1. On turn 2 Bot2 sacrifices Black Lotus for {B}{B}{B}, putting it in Bot2's graveyard, and casts Mind Stone
# ({2}) asking to delve a card: no graveyard card is offered, so the Lotus's mana pays all of it and the Lotus stays in Bot2's
# graveyard, nothing exiled. Bot1 loses no life for Bot2's spells either.

